From 21c264964f74da7d8459a21bbde80bb71b645f54 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ondrej Jirman <megi@xff.cz>
Date: Tue, 14 Jul 2026 22:45:45 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] usb: musb: Change quirk use from controller id to behavior
 description

Adding new controller with a slightly different behavior currently leads
to potentially having to modify quite lot of core code and having to
decipher interactions of various controllers. This is due to core driver
code having DMA controller specific quirks gated by the controller
name instead of a quirk flag that would gate a specific behavioral need
of a given controller.

It is better to have a behavior guard and just select a behavior by
requesting it in the musb platform ops. For one, it makes the code
easier to understand, and also it makes adding new platforms or support
easier for platforms like Allwinner SoCs which is implemented by one
musb glue, but Allwinner evolved different DMA implementations and
slight differences in their multitudes of SoC families.

This change will make it easier to support the DMA on Allwinner platform
in a clean way.

Signed-off-by: Ondrej Jirman <megi@xff.cz>
